ential management, or bio enrollment.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Client","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is an actor; a client’s lifetime is bound to the underlying ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/CTAP2\/Session","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The constructor takes four parameters that shape every ceremony:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"origin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the secure origin the client is bound to. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Origin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" enforces","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the W3C secure-context rule; the client refuses to sign for relying parties whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identifier doesn’t match.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"isPublicSuffix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — a closure into a Public Suffix List, used to validate that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the relying-party identifier is a registrable suffix of the origin’s effective","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"domain.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"enterpriseRpIds","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — relying-party identifiers allowed to receive","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"platform-managed enterprise attestation. When the request specifies","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/AttestationPreference\/enterprise","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", the client escalates to level 2","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(platform-managed) for RPs in this set, and uses level 1 (vendor-facilitated)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"otherwise.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"allowedExtensions","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the set of WebAuthn extensions the client will process.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Anything the relying party requests outside this set is dropped before reaching","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the authenticator. Defaults to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Extension","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"’s standard set.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"PIN and user verification are supplied per ceremony via ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Authorization","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out-of-band from the ceremony stream. Both ceremony methods return a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/StatusStream","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — drain it with ","type":"text"},{"code":"value()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for non-UI callers, or iterate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to drive cancel buttons and biometric prompts.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let client = WebAuthn.Client(","    session: session,","    origin: try .init(\"https:\/\/example.com\"),","    isPublicSuffix: { publicSuffixList.contains($0) }",")","","for try await status in await client.makeCredential(opts, authorization: .pin(\"1234\")) {","    switch status {","    case .processing:","        showSpinner()","    case .waitingForUser(let cancel):","        showTouchPrompt(onCancel: { Task { await can